{
  "title": "Platelet count\u2013volume coupling adds no robust CRP prediction benefit across NHANES cycles",
  "abstract": "In 4,122 NHANES 2005\u20132006 and 4,927 separately sampled 2007\u20132008 adults, adding a platelet count\u2013volume interaction to nonlinear standard-measure models increased target log-CRP MSE by 0.000169 (0.016%). The source-refit/target-PSU 95% interval [-0.001631, 0.007159] spans benefit and harm; no robust incremental predictive utility was established.",
